{% doc %}
  The CSS custom properties that size a carousel's slides before Swiper loads.

  ## The problem this solves

  `swiper.css` sets `.swiper-wrapper { display: flex }`, and it applies the
  moment the stylesheet parses. `.swiper-slide { flex-shrink: 0; width: 100% }`
  does *not* apply yet, because `assets/carousel.js` is what puts the
  `swiper-slide` class on the track's children, and it is a lazily loaded module.

  So between first paint and Swiper mounting, every slide is a flex item with the
  browser default `flex: 0 1 auto` — free to shrink. Twelve announcements squeeze
  into one row, and then snap to one slide when the module lands. That is the
  "it shows all 12 on page load" report, and no amount of Swiper configuration
  fixes it: Swiper is not running yet.

  The fix is to tell CSS what the slide width will be, in Liquid, in the markup.
  `base.css` has one generic rule that reads these properties; a section adds no
  CSS of its own, now or in future.

  ## Why these are not the `--columns-*` properties the grid already uses

  `--columns-desktop` is a whole-number column count for a CSS grid. These are
  Swiper's `slidesPerView`, which is a *fraction* whenever there is a peek. Same
  idea, different values, and overloading one name for both is how a 2.3-slide
  carousel ends up rendering as a 2-column grid for the first 200ms.

  ## Parameters

  Identical to `carousel-options` so a caller passes the same arguments to both:

    settings (object, required)
    columns_mobile / columns_tablet / columns_desktop (number)
    effect (string), peek_mobile (number), peek_desktop (number)
    space_between (number)  px. Omit to inherit the grid's own `--grid-gap-x`.

  @example
    <swiper-carousel
      style="{% render 'carousel-vars', settings: section.settings %}"
      data-options="{% render 'carousel-options', settings: section.settings %}">
{% enddoc %}

{%- capture slides_mobile -%}
  {%- render 'carousel-slides',
      settings: settings,
      viewport: 'mobile',
      columns_mobile: columns_mobile,
      effect: effect,
      peek_mobile: peek_mobile,
      peek_desktop: peek_desktop -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture slides_tablet -%}
  {%- render 'carousel-slides',
      settings: settings,
      viewport: 'tablet',
      columns_tablet: columns_tablet,
      effect: effect,
      peek_mobile: peek_mobile,
      peek_desktop: peek_desktop -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture slides_desktop -%}
  {%- render 'carousel-slides',
      settings: settings,
      viewport: 'desktop',
      columns_desktop: columns_desktop,
      effect: effect,
      peek_mobile: peek_mobile,
      peek_desktop: peek_desktop -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- liquid
  assign gap = space_between | default: -1 | plus: 0

  # `-1` is the sentinel for "the caller said nothing", because `0` is a real
  # value here. Unset, the gap falls through to the grid's own spacing, which is
  # the same number `carousel.js` measures for Swiper's `spaceBetween` — so the
  # slides do not resize when it mounts.
  if gap >= 0
    assign gap_value = gap | append: 'px'
  else
    assign gap_value = 'var(--grid-gap-x, 0rem)'
  endif
-%}

{%- capture vars -%}
  --carousel-slides-mobile: {{ slides_mobile | strip }};
  --carousel-slides-tablet: {{ slides_tablet | strip }};
  --carousel-slides-desktop: {{ slides_desktop | strip }};
  --carousel-gap: {{ gap_value }};
{%- endcapture -%}
{{- vars | strip_newlines | strip -}}
